Subject: [PATCH 2/2] docs(wayfinder): close ticket 07's grilling round, narrow
 ticket 08

/grill-me ticket 07 ran a multi-round grilling session to fully
specify the target architecture ticket 07 first sketched. Settled:

- The MDM machine ends at Reconcile, not GoldRefresh. Checked the
  actual code (mdm/export.py's DOMAIN_TO_TABLE,
  warehouse_orchestrator.py's gold-refresh handler) rather than
  assuming: Publish writes MDM's 5 entity tables directly; GoldRefresh
  rebuilds ~18 other, silver-derived gold tables unrelated to MDM.
  They're genuinely different jobs, not two names for the same step
  -- explains why residual_holds_graph already skips GoldRefresh
  today (no new bronze/silver capture in its own run).
- GoldRefresh renamed to FactPublishtoGold, stays its own separate
  machine, unaffected in count.
- One input contract, same shape for every caller, not one per
  caller.
- mdm_gold deleted outright -- already headless, fully redundant with
  the new MDM machine the moment it exists.
- bronze_seed_silver_gold's strict release-mode branch left untouched
  -- no equivalent anywhere else, forcing it in would recreate the
  exact "6 distinct shapes" problem this consolidation exists to fix.
- Checked (not assumed) what actually calls a seed machine today:
  load_history inlines its own seed steps directly, daily_incremental
  never seeds at all, and the standalone seed_universe/
  mdm_seed_universe machines have no pipeline caller at all -- they're
  ad-hoc operator tools. The merged seed machine keeps that role, and
  chains seed-universe -> mdm seed-universe in sequence (confirmed
  mdm seed-universe --source silver reads what warehouse seed-universe
  already wrote -- a real 2-stage pipeline, not two alternatives).
- One of daily_incremental's two inline tail copies is confirmed dead
  code from the retired bootstrap caller (write_warehouse_mdm_gold_
  definition's now-unreachable else branch) -- falls away for free
  during implementation, no separate ticket needed.

Ticket 08 narrowed accordingly: mdm_gold and the strict branch are
no longer part of its open question (settled directly by ticket 07);
its table now covers exactly the 4 remaining heads
(ownership_mdm_gold, silver_mdm_gold, bronze_seed_silver_gold's
default path, residual_holds_graph).

Map's Decisions-so-far entry for ticket 07 rewritten to reflect the
full settled shape. No code changed -- planning only.

